# cursor-byok project rules

## Git commit conventions

- Author: `genguzzz <genguzzz@qq.com>`
- Use English conventional commit format: `type(scope): subject`
  - type: `feat` | `fix` | `refactor` | `test` | `perf` | `docs` | `ci` | `chore`
  - scope: module name (e.g. `forwarder`, `menubar`, `mcp`, `prompt`, `ci`, `config`)
  - subject: concise English description, lowercase, no trailing period
- Body (optional): English, explain why and what changed
- No `Co-authored-by` or tool attribution lines
- No `--story=` or `--bug=` trailers
- No Chinese `【公版】` prefix or Chinese commit messages